.TH VWM 1 "November 2026" "OpenLook"
.SH NAME
vwm \- native overview of olwm virtual desktops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vwm
.RI [ XView-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vwm
opens an overview of the optional screen-sized desktops managed by olwm.
It is an XView application, not a replacement window manager.
Opening it in a single-desktop session enables a three-column, two-row grid.
Opening it again raises the existing overview, including when minimized.
The overview is visible on every desktop and uses the packaged vwm icon.
.SH CONTROLS
The compact window contains only the desktop grid, with dashed separators.
Click anywhere in a desktop, including over a miniature, to switch to it.
Drag a miniature window to another cell to move that window and its
dependent dialogs. Double-click a miniature to switch to its desktop,
restore it if minimized, raise it and give it focus.
.PP
Middle-click a miniature to show the window and its dependent dialogs on
every desktop. Middle-click it again to place them on the current desktop.
.PP
Control-Alt-Left, Control-Alt-Right, Control-Alt-Up and Control-Alt-Down
switch to adjacent desktops while multiple desktops are enabled.
.SH RESIZING
Resize the pager to change the grid. Each pane remains 80 by 72 pixels;
the window snaps to whole panes, with one to four columns and rows.
Growing adds panes when they fit. Existing panes retain their row and column.
Shrinking removes panes and moves windows
from removed desktops to the last remaining desktop.
Resizing to one pane disables desktop switching and brings all windows onto
the single desktop without changing their minimized state.
There is no Properties dialog; right-click does not open one.
.SH LIFETIME
Closing the overview leaves desktops and shortcuts active.
Desktop assignments, the current desktop and the grid survive Restart WM
on the same X server. Exiting olwm restores access to every client window.
Desktop assignments are not saved across new X server sessions.
.SH RESOURCES
.TP
.B OpenWindows.VirtualDesktop
Initial grid for a fresh olwm session, in columns-by-rows notation.
The default is 1x1. For example, 3x2 enables six desktops at startup.
A grid retained on the root window by Restart WM takes precedence.
.SH NOTES
Requires this project's updated olwm. Each desktop has the physical screen's
dimensions; continuous panning and windows spanning desktop cells are not
implemented. The overview polls geometry four times per second and displays
window outlines and names, not live application screenshots.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR olwm (1)
